{
	"title": "Intercaler une fraction décimale",
	"description": "Écrire une fraction décimale comprise entre deux autres (3/10 < 35/100 < 4/10 ; 43/100 < 435/1 000 < 44/100) ; toute fraction strictement entre les deux est juste",
	"grades": ["CM2"],
	"theme": "Fractions",
	"domain": "Apprivoiser",
	"subdomain": "Encadrer",
	"level": 7,
	"delay": 45,
	"status": "draft",
	"options": {
		"constraints": {
			"reducedFractions": "off",
			"spacesFromFourDigits": true
		}
	},
	"variations": [
		{
			"statement": "Écris une fraction décimale comprise entre ces deux fractions.\n\n$$\\frac{{{a}}}{10} < ? < \\frac{{{eval:a+1}}}{10}$$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "a",
					"expression": "1..49"
				}
			],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "\\frac{{{eval:10*a+5}}}{100}",
					"requiredForm": "fraction",
					"rulesSuffice": true,
					"validationRules": [
						{
							"type": "range",
							"min": "{{eval:a/10;d}}",
							"max": "{{eval:(a+1)/10;d}}",
							"inclusive": false
						}
					]
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"**Un rang plus loin.** $\\frac{{{a}}}{10} = \\frac{{{eval:10*a}}}{100}$ et $\\frac{{{eval:a+1}}}{10} = \\frac{{{eval:10*a+10}}}{100}$.",
					"Entre les deux, il y a $\\frac{{{eval:10*a+1}}}{100}$, $\\frac{{{eval:10*a+2}}}{100}$… jusqu'à $\\frac{{{eval:10*a+9}}}{100}$. Par exemple :",
					"$$\\frac{{{a}}}{10} < \\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{\\frac{{{eval:10*a+5}}}{100}} < \\frac{{{eval:a+1}}}{10}$$"
				]
			}
		},
		{
			"statement": "Écris une fraction décimale comprise entre ces deux fractions.\n\n$$\\frac{{{a}}}{100} < ? < \\frac{{{eval:a+1}}}{100}$$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "a",
					"expression": "1..299"
				}
			],
			"conditions": ["mod(a,10)!=0"],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "\\frac{{{eval:10*a+5}}}{1000}",
					"requiredForm": "fraction",
					"rulesSuffice": true,
					"validationRules": [
						{
							"type": "range",
							"min": "{{eval:a/100;d}}",
							"max": "{{eval:(a+1)/100;d}}",
							"inclusive": false
						}
					]
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"**Un rang plus loin.** $\\frac{{{a}}}{100} = \\frac{{{eval:10*a}}}{1000}$ et $\\frac{{{eval:a+1}}}{100} = \\frac{{{eval:10*a+10}}}{1000}$.",
					"Entre les deux, il y a $\\frac{{{eval:10*a+1}}}{1000}$, $\\frac{{{eval:10*a+2}}}{1000}$… jusqu'à $\\frac{{{eval:10*a+9}}}{1000}$. Par exemple :",
					"$$\\frac{{{a}}}{100} < \\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{\\frac{{{eval:10*a+5}}}{1000}} < \\frac{{{eval:a+1}}}{100}$$"
				]
			}
		}
	],
